        "description": "Reads a recording one of the person's other devices made (`file`, its name or identity in the person's files) through the run's door into the run's own folder, hears it on this computer with the Whisper model the person names, names each turn from the voices people enrolled (tool:enrol-a-voice-or-face), and writes one heard row per turn as tool:listen-for-a-while does, with `device` as the device and times counted from `at` (when the device began recording; now when left out). The same `listening` name continues an earlier listening's unknown voices. The person's recording rules and the listening's listening-switch row are asked as for a live listening. The copy read for hearing is deleted once heard; the person's file is left where it is. Every answer lists what leaves this computer and what stays.",
